# Round 87, and this one is a debt rather than a new file.  Sweeping every
# evidence_ref and source_ref in the hypothesis ledger against check-ignore --
# which is what the new test beside verify_hypothesis_ledger.py now does on
# every run -- found this report ignored since the day it was written on
# 2026-08-14, while TWO ACTIVE ENTRIES, HYP-PF-008 and HYP-PF-010, cite it as
# evidence.  Nothing was wrong with the file and nothing in either entry has to
# change: a fresh clone simply did not contain the document those two claims
# rest on, and no check in this repository was looking.  It is added rather
# than the references removed, because the references are correct.
!/reports/PF_RE_V107_to_V110_Stateful_Inventory_and_ActionItem_Capture_20260814.md

# DAMAGE-ENCODER-001 / DAMAGE-DISPATCH-001 (round 90, HYP-PF-024) -- the
# encoder's offline verifier, the headless replay that drives the sweep through
# the real dispatcher, the closing report, and the two design documents the
# ledger entry cites as evidence.  The drafts are listed here rather than
# dropped from evidence_refs for the reason round 87 wrote down: the references
# were the part that was correct, and a claim whose evidence a fresh clone does
# not contain is not evidence.  The R90 static document in particular carries
# the byte tables that answer the version byte and the construction path, which
